// - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -
// Filename:	TS040 Flood Array PCB draft 0.5test
// Project:		VSC80,90,900
// Author:      Foster & Freeman Ltd - Paul Evans
// Modified:    29/07/24
//
// Description: Using the nano inside TE209 to control the relay (x2) for 5V regulator  to the PICKkit4 and the power on button.
// Check current fw and if not expect updates the fw. 
// Steps 3 to 4.6 are setup/logic for the test box itself
// - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -

[0] force FAIL by default to avoid IMPORTANT message below.

#1: Enter operator initials and PCB serial number:
a. Enter operator intials.
b. Enter serial number into the box below.
IMPORTANT: Observe ESD precautions for handling ESD sensitive devices.  
DISPLAY: 260-022.png
CLICK_OK:

#2: Equipment Setup 1
a. Using TE159 connect the PSU to the VSC90 Controller Test Box(TE209).
b. Connect the PC (via USB) to K5 on the Test box (TE209).
c. Connect the PC (via USB) to the TENMA Programmable PSU.
d. Connect the PC to the LED Test Box with Web Camera (TE086).
DISPLAY: FloodSetup.png
CLICK_OK:


#3: Equipment Setup 2
a. Connect the UUT to the VSC90 Controller Test Box(TE209).
b. Connect the VSC90 Flood Array PCB to the PCB Fixture (TE217).
c. Place the UUT inside the LED Test Box with Web Camera (TE086).
d. Set the TENMA Programmable PSU power switch to on.
CLICK_OK:
EXE: OpenWinCam.bat
CONNECT: TE209				// Connect to the Nano in the TE209
COMMAND: TE209 OUT RC7 1 	// TURN Power button RELAY OFF
COMMAND: TE209 OUT RC6 1 	// TURN Pickit RELAY OFF
CONNECT: TENMAPSU
IF_NOT:
GOTO: #3: 

#4: Configure the PSU
COMMAND: TENMAPSU OUT0
COMMAND: TENMAPSU OCP1
COMMAND: TENMAPSU OCPSET1:500
COMMAND: TENMAPSU VSET1:12.00
COMMAND: TENMAPSU ISET1:1.00
COMMAND: TENMAPSU OUTCH1:1

#4.1: Power on the test box.
COMMAND: TE209 OUT RC7 0 		// TURN power button RELAY ON
DELAY: 500
COMMAND: TE209 OUT RC7 1 		// TURN power button RELAY OFF
COMMAND: TENMAPSU IOUT1?
READLINE: TENMAPSU PSUcurrent
The returned voltage is =  %PSUcurrent%
RANGE: %PSUcurrent% 0.060 0.015 // Set the range as per TS014_TEST_SEQUENCER_scripts.docx 						
IF: 							// True result, current is good
GOTO: #4.2: 
IMPORTANT: This test has failed, check the power button has been pressed, power supply, USB connection and the ftdi chip.		
PASS_FAIL: #4.1:


#4.2: Connect to the test box
a. If error message below is diplayed, then click OK to continue. 
.
ERROR on line 71, CONNECT_ VSC90 - Not available.
DELAY: 9000 					// GIVE TIME FOR THE PC AND NEW ftdi TO WAKE
CONNECT: VSC90	 				// Test connection to the FDTI chip
IF_NOT: 						// If wrong FTDI porgram
GOTO: #4.3: 					// Reprogram the FTDI and PIC
GOTO: #4.6: 					// FTDI is correct now check the PIC is programmed correctly 


#4.3: program the FTDI 
EXE: ftdi_programmer_vsc90.exe
#4.3.1: program the PIC
COMMAND: TE209 OUT RC6 0 		// TURN PICKIT RELAY ON
EXE: VSC90FWself_powered.bat
DELAY: 2000
COMMAND: TE209 OUT RC6 1 		// TURN PICKIT RELAY OFF
COMMAND: TENMAPSU OUTCH1:0
DELAY: 2000
GOTO: #4.4: // 

#4.3.2: program the PIC attempt 2 
DISCONNECT: VSC90
COMMAND: TE209 OUT RC6 0 		// TURN PICKIT RELAY ON
EXE: VSC90FWself_powered.bat
DELAY: 2000
COMMAND: TE209 OUT RC6 1 		// TURN PICKIT RELAY OFF
COMMAND: TENMAPSU OUTCH1:0
DELAY: 2000

#4.4:  Press the I/O Power button and turn on the test box
COMMAND: TENMAPSU OUTCH1:1
COMMAND: TE209 OUT RC7 0 		// TURN power button RELAY ON
DELAY: 500
COMMAND: TE209 OUT RC7 1 		// TURN power button RELAY OFF
COMMAND: TENMAPSU IOUT1?
READLINE: TENMAPSU PSUcurrent
The returned voltage is =  %PSUcurrent%
RANGE: %PSUcurrent% 0.060 0.015 // Set the range as per TS014_TEST_SEQUENCER_scripts.docx 				
IF_NOT: 
GOTO: #4.4: 					// There is fault with the current reading, go back and try again 

#4.5: Connect again
DELAY: 7000 					// GIVE TIME FOR THE pc AND NEW ftdi TO WAKE
CONNECT: VSC90
IF_NOT: 
GOTO: #4: 						// GO BACK TO THE START

#4.6: PCB Program version check.
COMMAND: VSC90  TYPE 			// Check connection to the PIC chip
READLINE: VSC90  TYPE
Returned product is = %TYPE%
[%TYPE% STR_EQ VSC90] 			// Evaluates the FW by checking inside the [] and set true or false flag
IF:
GOTO: #5: 						// Checks and programming complete goto the start of tests
ELSE: 							// PIC is not programmed correctly still
IMPORTANT: Cannot program the test box (PIC). Please check connections to the PIC Kit and PCB.
CLICK_OK:
GOTO: #4.3.2: 					// Try programming the PIC again


#5: Test box f/W  version check
COMMAND: VSC90  BUILD
READLINE: VSC90  BUILD
Returned Version is = %BUILD%
ELSE:
Bad result . . . No communication to PIC device


#6: Voltage check
COMMAND: VSC90 READVOLTS 
READLINE: VSC90 READVOLTS 
Returned Voltage is = %READVOLTS%
RANGE: %READVOLTS% 12000 50					
SUB: TestPassOrFail


#7: Tests the I2C to the EEPROM and 3.3V supply
COMMAND: VSC90  ENUM
READLINE: VSC90  ENUM
Check the expected result is a match.
Expected result is = LFLOOD,ZOOM,EEPROM,
Returned result is = %ENUM%
[%ENUM% STR_EQ LFLOOD,ZOOM,EEPROM,]// evaluates inside the [] and set true or false flag
SUB: TestPassOrFail // sends the outcome to flag to the subroutine for evaluation


#8: Check white LED's 3 & 4
COMMAND: VSC90 W12 1023
DELAY: 1500
COMMAND: TENMAPSU IOUT1?
READLINE: TENMAPSU PSUcurrent
The returned current is =  %PSUcurrent%
RANGE: %PSUcurrent% 0.240 0.010 // set the range as per TS014_TEST_SEQUENCER_scripts.docx 						
SUB: TestPassOrFail


#9: Check white LED 9
COMMAND: VSC90 OVD 2 1023
DELAY: 1500
COMMAND: TENMAPSU IOUT1?
READLINE: TENMAPSU PSUcurrent
The returned current is =  %PSUcurrent%
RANGE: %PSUcurrent% 0.170 0.010 // set the range as per TS014_TEST_SEQUENCER_scripts.docx 						
SUB: TestPassOrFail


#10: Check white LED 10
COMMAND: VSC90 OVD 4 750
DELAY: 1500
COMMAND: TENMAPSU IOUT1?
READLINE: TENMAPSU PSUcurrent
The returned current is =  %PSUcurrent%
RANGE: %PSUcurrent% 0.135 0.010 // set the range as per TS014_TEST_SEQUENCER_scripts.docx 						
SUB: TestPassOrFail

#11: Check UV LED's 7, 8, 13
COMMAND: VSC90 UV365 1023
DELAY: 1500
COMMAND: TENMAPSU IOUT1?
READLINE: TENMAPSU PSUcurrent
The returned current is =  %PSUcurrent%
RANGE: %PSUcurrent% 0.410 0.010 // set the range as per TS014_TEST_SEQUENCER_scripts.docx 						
SUB: TestPassOrFail


#12: Check  IR780 LED's 6 & 5
COMMAND: VSC90 IR780 1023
DELAY: 1500
COMMAND: TENMAPSU IOUT1?
READLINE: TENMAPSU PSUcurrent
The returned current is =  %PSUcurrent%
RANGE: %PSUcurrent% 0.190 0.010 // set the range as per TS014_TEST_SEQUENCER_scripts.docx 						
SUB: TestPassOrFail


#13: Check  IR850 LED's D1 & D2
COMMAND: VSC90 IR850 1023
DELAY: 1500
COMMAND: TENMAPSU IOUT1?
READLINE: TENMAPSU PSUcurrent
The returned current is =  %PSUcurrent%
RANGE: %PSUcurrent% 0.240 0.010 // set the range as per TS014_TEST_SEQUENCER_scripts.docx 						
SUB: TestPassOrFail


#14: Check  IR940 LED's D3 & D4
COMMAND: VSC90 IR940 1023
DELAY: 1500
COMMAND: TENMAPSU IOUT1?
READLINE: TENMAPSU PSUcurrent
The returned current is =  %PSUcurrent%
RANGE: %PSUcurrent% 0.230 0.010 // set the range as per TS014_TEST_SEQUENCER_scripts.docx 						
SUB: TestPassOrFail


#15: Check  IR980 LED's 1 & 2
COMMAND: VSC90 IR980 1023
DELAY: 1500
COMMAND: TENMAPSU IOUT1?
READLINE: TENMAPSU PSUcurrent
The returned current is =  %PSUcurrent%
RANGE: %PSUcurrent% 0.163 0.010 // set the range as per TS014_TEST_SEQUENCER_scripts.docx 						
SUB: TestPassOrFail


#16: Test complete
COMMAND: VSC90 If#	// turn off any LEDs still on: 
#17: Test complete
IF: %FAILED% > 0
GOTO: #Failed:
ELSE: #Passed:

#Failed: a test failed
This PCB has failed to pass all Tests
Check the Log file for more details on the failed test(s).
IMPORTANT: This PCB has failed to pass all Tests
DISPLAY: test_failed.png
CLICK_OK:
GOTO: #QUIT:

#Passed: Test's Complete
a. All tests instructions have been completed and a log file created.
b. Click OK to finish and power OFF.
DISPLAY: AllTestsPassed.png
CLICK_OK:

#QUIT:
COMMAND: TENMAPSU VSET1:0.00
COMMAND: TENMAPSU ISET1:0.00
COMMAND: TENMAPSU OUT0
DISCONNECT: TENMAPSU
DISCONNECT: TE209
DISCONNECT: VSC90
EXE: CloseWinCam.bat
// End of file
